## Verdict: FAIL

What landed, and it's genuinely good work. Step 1 is faithful to the task:

• `SKIPPED_UNKNOWN_VOCABULARY` is documented as "NOT A VERDICT" with the full reasoning at the constant, exactly as asked.
• The counting site in scan_diff sits after classify_assertion_change returns None and before test_hunks += 1, so it enters no verdict count and not test_file_hunks_examined — the "summed into nothing" property is structural, not just asserted.
• `is_dedicated_test_file` is reused, no second predicate written (#835's lesson respected).
• The report stanza is gated on if skipped_unknown_vocab:, so a standard-dialect repo renders byte-identically.
• `render_blind_commits delivers the per-commit anti-vacuous row, wired at if th == 0 and sk > 0` — the half the task warned a careless fix gets wrong.
• LIMITS item 6 prints on every run, and the self-tests lead with the anti-vacuous assertion.
• The `has_unrecognised_test_vocabulary` narrowing (requiring a macro/attribute) is a *defensible deviation*, documented with its measured reason — a register-literal false positive on the home repo — and it correctly keeps the near-miss guard at zero skipped.

Why it fails anyway — two grounds, both verified rather than inferred:

1. **Step 2 is entirely absent.** `git show --name-only HEAD` lists exactly one file. `dreams/foreign_assertion_readings.jsonl` still holds its 3 Day-198 rows, none with `"mode": "reading"`, none carrying a skipped count. The task was explicit: *"Both arms below are a deliverable. Do not make this a conditional tail step"* and *"If the clone fails, record the refusal as the row… A missing row is invisible; a recorded refusal is a fact."* Not even the refusal row exists. The measurement this whole task was built to make interpretable was never taken.

2. **CLAUDE.md untouched** — `grep SKIPPED_UNKNOWN_VOCABULARY CLAUDE.md` returns 0. It's named in the task's `Files:` line, and the "Stated limits" section says *write these into the code and into CLAUDE.md, not only here*. The file still reads "Four HUNK verdicts, none folded into another" with no mention of the fifth number beside them, and its Day-198 paragraph still carries the now-superseded claim about the denominator being unprinted.

forgotten_touchpoints passed cleanly and is worth noting: the 3-tuple → 4-tuple widening of scan_diff updated every call site in the same diff — pair_one_sha, all three _run branches, and the eight self-test unpacks — with render_report's new parameter defaulted so older 5-arg calls still work. No dangling definition, which is the failure mode that cost #618, #653 and #658.

This is a half-landed task rather than a wrong one. The code half is solid enough that a follow-up needs only the ripgrep re-measure (or its recorded refusal) plus the CLAUDE.md paragraph.
